::ENG1_U04_L05_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG1.W.03] Prompt: Finding: Students with quiet study access reported fewer homework distractions. Which sentence best integrates the finding?
{
=A. A student survey found that quiet study access was linked to fewer homework distractions. #Correct. This introduces the source finding clearly and formally.
~B. Quiet rooms are awesome and homework is stuff. #Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
~C. Students and homework and quiet. #Incorrect. This is a fragment, not source integration.
~D. The source proves everything forever. #Incorrect. This is exaggerated and unclear.
}

::ENG1_U04_L05_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG1.W.03] Prompt: Which transition best adds a related finding?
{
~A. However, #Incorrect. This signals contrast, not addition.
=B. In addition, #Correct. This transition adds another related idea.
~C. In conclusion, #Incorrect. This signals an ending.
~D. Instead, #Incorrect. This signals replacement or contrast.
}

::ENG1_U04_L05_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG1.W.04] Prompt: Draft: "The source is super good and says tutoring helps and stuff." Which revision has the best academic tone?
{
~A. The source is awesome and totally proves stuff. #Incorrect. This remains informal and vague.
~B. Tutoring is nice because the source says so. #Incorrect. This is still vague and weak.
=C. The survey suggests that tutoring may support student confidence. #Correct. This revision is formal, specific, and source-based.
~D. Tutoring stuff is cool. #Incorrect. This is informal and unclear.
}

::ENG1_U04_L05_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG1.W.03] Prompt: Which sentence best explains a source finding?
{
~A. The source is about a thing. #Incorrect. This is too vague to explain the finding.
~B. Source, students, homework, quiet. #Incorrect. This is a fragment list.
~C. I liked the source because it was interesting. #Incorrect. This is personal opinion.
=D. The finding suggests that quiet spaces may help students complete homework with fewer distractions. #Correct. This explains the finding clearly.
}

::ENG1_U04_L05_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Prompt: Which sentence uses standard English?
{
~A. The source say students completes homework. #Incorrect. The verbs do not agree with the subjects.
=B. The source says students complete homework more often in quiet spaces. #Correct. The sentence uses standard subject-verb agreement.
~C. The source saying students completes homework. #Incorrect. This is not a complete standard sentence.
~D. Students completes homework quiet spaces. #Incorrect. The sentence is grammatically unclear.
}
